{"name":"Charybdis","hex":"#16a3cb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Charybdis","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A dangerous whirlpool on the coast of Sicily opposite Scylla on the Italian coast.","A personification of the above whirlpool as a female monster."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Charybdis"}],"entries":[{"title":"Charybdis","blocks":[{"text":"Charybdis is a sea monster in Greek mythology. Along with the sea monster Scylla, she appears as a challenge to epic characters such as Odysseus, Jason, and Aeneas. The descriptions of Greek mythical chroniclers and Greek historians locate her in the Strait of Messina."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Johann_Heinrich_F%C3%BCssli_054.jpg/330px-Johann_Heinrich_F%C3%BCssli_054.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charybdis","wikidata":"Q192082"},{"title":"Charybdis (crab)","blocks":[{"text":"Charybdis is a genus of swimming crabs in the family Portunidae. It is named after the monster Charybdis of Greek mythology."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Charybdis_japonica.jpg/330px-Charybdis_japonica.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charybdis_(crab)","wikidata":"Q2961314"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Strait_of_Messina.jpg/330px-Strait_of_Messina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Strait_of_Messina.jpg/330px-Strait_of_Messina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Strait of Messina, with Scylla (underlined in red) and Charybdis on the opposite shores","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStrait_of_Messina.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wiki